From 53248f67c605a2ebbc52eed51e87b071eeb6c416 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jgrizon
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 15:50:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gpu: show the Series S scene plane and draw the UI over it by
 default

On Series S the title presents two planes: plane 0 the scene at the
title's output size, plane 1 the 3840x2160 UI (credits, subtitles, the
HUD over black). The window showed the plane whose first resource had
the most pixels, i.e. the UI, so the opening scenes came out black with
text over them; the blend that would draw the scene was opt-in.

Ported from pragyaangaur/VIctory-macOS 8faee56 (#517), which is how
upstream renders the opening: show the first plane with a known
resource, and blend the other plane over it unless
VICTORY_PRESENT_COMPOSITE=0. VICTORY_PRESENT_PLANE still picks a plane.
Series X presents one plane, so nothing changes there.

Opening save, release build: before, the screen stayed black at about
3,826 draws a frame; after, the night scene with lights at about 4,425.

Generated by Mistral Vibe.

Co-Authored-By: Mistral Vibe <vibe@mistral.ai>
