 ## Presented planes
 
-On Series S the game presents two planes. Plane 0 is a 1920x1080 overlay and plane 1 is the 3840x2160 picture (#15). The window shows the plane whose first resource has the most pixels, and `VICTORY_PRESENT_PLANE=<n>` picks another one. With `VICTORY_PRESENT_COMPOSITE=1` the other plane is also blended over the shown one by a compute pass (`victory-gpu/src/composite.rs`), scaled to it and using its alpha as straight alpha. The blend is off by default until a run with the game shows that the overlay is clear where the picture should show.
+On Series S the game presents two planes (#15). Plane 0 is the scene, at the title's output size (1920x1080, or the size `VICTORY_OUTPUT` sets), and plane 1 is the 3840x2160 UI: credits, subtitles and the HUD over black. The window shows the first plane, and `VICTORY_PRESENT_PLANE=<n>` picks another one. The other plane is blended over the shown one by a compute pass (`victory-gpu/src/composite.rs`), scaled to it and using its alpha as straight alpha. `VICTORY_PRESENT_COMPOSITE=0` turns the blend off. Series X presents one plane, so neither changes anything there.
 
